From ff0e4867797eedd1d6054c624b7f55598730adae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 02:28:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] media: iris: ROG5: encoder bring-up guards: markers, DMA
 window, errors, start gating

The k115 trial's H.264 encode hung the ROG Phone 5 at session start with
nothing in the surviving log: the in-memory trace dies with the SoC. For
the next, dedicated encoder trial (the encoder stays unregistered unless
experimental_encoder=1, patch 0163):

- markers (module parameter, default off): a warning-level line before
  and after runtime suspend/resume, each core init step, every command
  sent (property id and first payload words), and the first six buffer
  packets after each SESSION_INIT. Printed synchronously to the consoles,
  so netconsole (built as a module for this) gets them off the phone
  before a hang.
- The HFI trace keeps 16 words per packet (an encoder ETB's extradata
  fields).
- Every firmware-visible buffer (input, output, internal, EOS, HFI queues,
  SFR) must lie in the non-secure IOVA window [cp_size, dma_mask + 1),
  i.e. [0x25800000, 0xe0000000) here, end included; anything else is
  refused before it is sent.
- ETB/FTB packets are zero-initialised (extradata_buffer, data).
- Property setters: a failed command, a dead firmware or a failed
  allocation (-EIO, -ETIMEDOUT, -ENOMEM) now fails the stream-on; -EINVAL
  stays "not applicable" (setters use it, e.g. bitrate before streaming).
  A failed clock/bandwidth vote fails the stream-on and encoder queueing.
- Experimental SM8350 encoder only: LOAD_RESOURCES/START wait until both
  ports streamed on (the CAPTURE port's properties, frame rate included,
  used to arrive after START when the raw port streamed on first), the
  work route (4 pipes) is set explicitly before LOAD as stock does, and no
  buffer reaches the firmware before the instance is STREAMING. A
  CAPTURE-only stream-off (STOP/RELEASE) followed by a CAPTURE stream-on
  while the raw port still streams loads and starts the session again.

ROG5: patch 0165, kernel k116. Not in upstream.
